# Zyko's PC Checker 4 — Privacy Policy
Effective September 20, 2026. Applies to version 4.0.0.

## What an examination accesses

Standard scans examine accessible file metadata and relevant technical content,
running processes, installed software, execution traces, Roblox configuration and
logs, account identifiers, download records, Windows history and removable-device
artifacts. File paths, usernames, account IDs, hashes and timestamps can identify
people or reveal their activity. Ordinary personal documents and media receive
limited type checks; a disguised executable may receive deeper examination.

Expanded collection is optional and requires an acknowledgement before each
scan. It additionally collects process command lines and parent relationships,
service and driver settings, scheduled task actions, DNS cache entries, WMI
persistence settings, available Amcache records, restore-point metadata, Windows
event messages, PowerShell command history and bounded NTFS journal/file-reference
records. These sources can reveal private activity. Command lines and saved
commands may contain secrets entered by other software or by a person; automatic
redaction is not guaranteed. Do not enable this scope without appropriate authority.

The separate memory option reads bounded samples of Roblox executable memory
pages and records region metadata and PE-header indicators. Raw memory samples
are discarded after inspection and are not included in reports. This is not a
complete memory dump or comprehensive injection detector. Protected sources,
unsupported formats, missing permissions and collection limits affect coverage.

Custom YARA rules inspect eligible executable and script bytes locally. Rule
matches, names and tags may be reported. Rules are operator supplied; their
accuracy is not guaranteed. Do not put private information in rule names or tags.

## Storage, sharing and network connections

Collected inventory and findings remain in application memory until the session
ends unless the operator exports a JSON or HTML report. Exports include the
expanded inventory when enabled, collection limitations and a source timeline.
Exports are not encrypted by the application. The local scan cache under
`%LOCALAPPDATA%/ZykoPCChecker/scan-cache.sqlite3` retains file paths, identity
metadata, hashes and cached analysis to accelerate later scans. A configured
custom cache path takes precedence. Closing the app does not delete this cache.

The app does not automatically upload scan evidence, history, memory samples or
reports. Its update checks and downloads contact the configured release service;
that service receives normal network metadata, such as the connecting IP address.
Windows signature validation may use Windows-managed certificate services.
Sharing an exported report is a separate action controlled by the operator.

## Retention and control

You may decline expanded collection, stop a running scan or close the app. A
cancelled report can contain evidence already collected. Delete unwanted exported
reports and, after closing the app, the local cache and its SQLite sidecar files
to remove application-retained data. Other recipients and operating-system backups
may retain copies; the app cannot delete those remotely. There is no application
cloud account or central evidence store in this build.

Operators must restrict report access, choose and communicate a retention period,
and provide an appropriate contact for questions or deletion requests before
collecting another person's data. The application does not know the operator's
contact details and cannot answer requests on their behalf.

## Accuracy and changes

Collection is broader in version 4, but a greater amount of personal data does
not guarantee better detection. Contextual activity is not proof of misconduct.
Coverage records distinguish unavailable, partial and unsupported checks.
Future changes to collection require corresponding policy and interface updates.
